# Picacho's listing in app stores (Flathub, GNOME Software, KDE Discover),
# from packaging/flatpak/tech.pinal.picacho.metainfo.xml. Not shown in
# Picacho itself; scripts/release/l10n.py writes the translations into the
# listing. Plain text: no { } placeholders.

# One line under the app's name
listing-summary = Fast, native email for every inbox you have.

listing-description = Picacho is a fast, native email client written in Rust with GPUI. It runs without Electron or a webview, and it works with the mail you already have. Gray surfaces, a three-pane layout, rounded controls, and light and dark palettes with a choice of theme colors keep the focus on your mail.

